        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): tighten grepSchema context/limit from Type.Number to Type.Integer",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #105822\n\n**Problem**: `grepSchema.context` and `grepSchema.limit` use `Type.Number`, accepting fractional values like `1.5` or `10.5` that are semantically invalid for context lines and match counts.\n\n**Solution**: Change both fields to `Type.Integer` so schema validation rejects floats before reaching tool logic. Export `grepSchema` from the module so tests validate against the production schema instead of a reconstructed copy. This follows the same pattern applied to the `ls` tool schema in PR #105827.\n\n**What changed**: Two characters in `src/agents/sessions/tools/grep.ts:44-49` — `Type.Number` → `Type.Integer` for both `context` and `limit`. The test now imports and validates against the exported production `grepSchema`. Removed standalone `_validate_grep.mjs` script from repo root. Rebased branch onto latest upstream/main to resolve branch-behind-main status.\n\n**NOT changed**: Tool execution behavior, default values (context=0, limit=100), `normalizePositiveLimit` clamping, any other schema field, or tool registration. Existing grep tests continue to pass. The standalone `_validate_grep.mjs` script was removed as redundant — the production schema test covers the same ground.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Schema-level rejection of float `context` and `limit` values via the production `grepSchema`.\n**Real environment tested**: Linux x64, Node.js 25.9.0, OpenClaw `main@HEAD` with this patch applied.\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**: `pnpm test src/agents/sessions/tools/grep.limit-schema.test.ts` then direct schema validation via `node --import tsx/esm`\n**After-fix evidence**: Test + terminal output both pass (see Tests and terminal output below).\n**Observed result after the fix**: `Check(grepSchema, { pattern: \"foo\", context: 1.5, limit: 50 })` returns `false`; `Check(grepSchema, { pattern: \"foo\", context: 3, limit: 10.5 })` returns `false`. All four validation scenarios pass as shown in the terminal output below.\n**What was not tested**: End-to-end grep execution (covered by existing `grep.stream-errors.test.ts`); real OpenClaw agent runtime integration is out of scope for this schema-level gate.\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n```\n$ pnpm test src/agents/sessions/tools/grep.limit-schema.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n RUN  v4.1.9\n\n ✓ |unit-fast| rejects float context and limit — validates against production grepSchema\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\n\n$ node --import tsx/esm -e \"...\"\n\n  PASS {\"pattern\":\"foo\",\"context\":3,\"limit\":50} → true\n  PASS {\"pattern\":\"foo\",\"context\":1.5,\"limit\":50} → false\n  PASS {\"pattern\":\"foo\",\"context\":3,\"limit\":10.5} → false\n  PASS {\"pattern\":\"foo\"} → true\n4/4 passed\n```\n\nValidated against the exported production `grepSchema`:\n\n| Input | Expected | Result |\n|-------|----------|--------|\n| `{ pattern: \"foo\", context: 3, limit: 50 }` | ✅ accept | passed |\n| `{ pattern: \"foo\", context: 1.5, limit: 50 }` | ❌ reject (float context) | passed |\n| `{ pattern: \"foo\", context: 3, limit: 10.5 }` | ❌ reject (float limit) | passed |\n| `{ pattern: \"foo\" }` (optionals omitted) | ✅ accept | passed |\n\nThe branch was rebased onto the latest upstream/main to resolve the stale-base issue flagged in the initial review.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible — integers previously accepted by `Type.Number` remain accepted by `Type.Integer`\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations — production schema validated directly\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation — schema is self-documenting via TypeBox types\n- [x] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary\n\n---\nmerge-risk: 🚨 compatibility — narrow schema contract change (float → integer only), accepted as intentional.\n",
        "branch": "fix/scan-20260713-7-grep-type-integer",
